  "title": "Mashemeji Derby: Banter at the Local",
  "category": "social",
  "difficulty": "advanced",
  "level": 10,
  "order": 1003,
  "theme": "sports",
  "culturalNote": "Gor Mahia vs AFC Leopards — the \"Mashemeji Derby\" (the brothers-in-law derby) — is Kenya's biggest football rivalry. The nickname comes from the many marriages between Luo and Luhya families, the clubs' traditional fan bases. Watching at a local bar or kibanda is a festival of trash talk, proverbs and idioms: \"Akose achekwe!\" (of course he'll score — he'd never live it down), \"Maji yakimwagika hayazoleki\" (spilled water can't be gathered — what's done is done), \"Asiyekubali kushindwa si mshindani\" (a sore loser is no real competitor).",
  "startingPoint": "Sunday afternoon at a sports bar in Nairobi. You support Gor Mahia; your friend Wafula is a die-hard AFC Leopards fan.",
